  "scope": "# Maintainer brief\nTask `74a14031dc79`, generator version `3.0.0`; final source SHA-256 `11a12a0ad29bcf2ddc4bd744b1fc34ab0e1cf6fb30bf3ae9f966eaa8ca8078a3`.\nDefect: the selected generator accepted Boolean/float/string seeds and sample indices plus negative sample indices; before `defect_lint` reproduced 33 warnings.\nRepair: strict literal-integer validation was added in `generator.py`, with a new focused regression file; lawful deterministic generation is unchanged.\nAuthority: no Racket rule, canonical label, target text, or `RULE_HASH = 582367af483f` changed.\nChecks: the final after battery is 12/12 green; profile support is 30/60 exact hits (easy 11, medium 8, hard 11).\nTask tests: 86/86 pass both in the working review and after fresh patch replay, including 17 proposed-parametric tests and 11 strict-scalar cases.\nLessons: three demonstrations per query; 300 production lessons and all 1,200 held-out query rotations have zero declared-rival ambiguity, with 1,197 unique inputs.\nParametric assessment: a separate proposed `occupancy_rule={or,xor,and}` prototype has 3/3 complete episodes, 9/9 rival checks, zero ambiguity, and 6/6 canonical OR replays.\nRemaining limits: finite rivals and three prototype seeds are not universal uniqueness evidence; the variants remain unapproved and outside production.\nAcceptance: routine for the validation repair and task-local prototype; audit finding `09647f283588` is findings-only and intentionally unpatched.\n\n## What changed",
